      "text": "Rajya Sabha MP Vikram Sahney, one of the seven leaders who quit the Aam Aadmi Party, revealed that me met with AAP national convenor Arvind Kejriwal days before the merger with the BJP.\n\nIn an interview, industralist and philanthropist Sahney said, “I met with Arvind Kejriwal on Wednesday. I told him about our plans...” Sahney said that he had warned Kejriwal that even “one-two MPs” leaving would lead to eventually the two-thirds threshold — the mark required to avoid disqualification under the anti-defection law.\n\n#AAP #ArvindKejriwal \n\nKnow more 🔗 https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/frustration-was-growing-rs-member-vikramjit-sahney-on-what-he-told-kejriwal-at-meet-before-7-aap-mps-big-move-101777194933935.html",
